<title>USA: Yamanouchi US unit drops animal drug study.</title>
<headline>Yamanouchi US unit drops animal drug study.</headline>
<text>
<p>WASHINGTON, June 19 ( Reuter)- Yamanouchi USA Inc said Thursday it had dropped plans for an animal study of a drug intended for the treatment of osteoporosis in humans, mainly because of protests by animal rights groups.</p>
<p>The company said it would contact the U.S. Food &amp; Drug Administration to determine what, if any, alternative studies would be acceptable to the FDA to assist in obtaining approval of the drug.</p>
<p>Yamanouchi USA is a unit of Yamanouchi Pharmaceutical Co Ltd.</p>
</text>
